Session: 751c1ce8cd6b432a863242cfb23c0300
Goal: Finalize and validate the existing uncommitted work in this repository: the fix for DOG-039 (see the DOG-039 entry in dogfood/findings/FINDINGS.md and its change_log.md entry). A Codex usage-limit stop line ("You've hit your usage limit. ... try again at 8:01 PM.") was classified AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED because the transcript-wide fallback matched the bare word "unauthorized" in rules prose. The change adds an anchored SESSION_LIMIT pattern for that stop line in src/howlplane/control_plane/synthesis/provider_pool.py and replaces the fallback's bare "unauthorized" marker with "401 unauthorized"; tests are in tests/test_usage_limit_classification.py.

If the existing change is correct and complete, report IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS: NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED with reasons; otherwise fix only what is wrong and add tests. HowlPlane runs `make test-full` itself and supplies the result, so run only targeted tests. Reviewers: try to falsify the fix: a genuine authentication failure (any CLI) that would now be missed, other providers whose usage-limit wording still falls through to the auth markers, whether the new pattern can match ordinary model prose given that only last lines are considered, and whether the readiness cache test proves the stated behavior.
